@event aid_notice
# en: The Hardship Notice
title [a50a45] = 困难补助告示
# en: {A small notice by the bursar's door reads "Hardship fund. Applications in writing. All circumstances considered."|The hardship notice again, under a new one about lost owls.|Someone has underlined "all circumstances" on the hardship notice.} {~Three students are pretending not to queue.|The ink on the forms is still wet.|The bursar's door is ajar.}
text [c8f698] = {财务官门边贴着一张小告示：“困难基金。书面申请。各种情况均予考虑。”|又是那张困难补助告示，上面盖了一张寻找走失猫头鹰的新告示。|有人在困难补助告示的“各种情况”下面画了线。}{~三个学生假装没在排队。|表格上的墨迹还没干。|财务官的门半开着。}
# en: A notice pinned beside the bursar's office door, half covered by a newer notice about lost owls, a queue of three students pretending not to queue.
scene [b50ea8] = 财务官办公室门边钉着一张告示，被一张关于走失猫头鹰的新告示盖住了一半，三个学生假装没在排队。
# en: Fill in the forms
opt.left.label [396803] = 填写表格
# en: {~Four pages. One asks you to list everything you own. It doesn't take long, and that is the hard part.|You fill in the forms at a library table with your arm around them so nobody can see.}
opt.left.say.1 [ce29b8] = {~四页纸。其中一页要你列出你拥有的所有东西。没花多少时间，这才是难受的地方。|你在图书馆的桌子上填表，用胳膊挡着，不让别人看见。}
# en: Not yet
opt.right.label [8dd27c] = 先不了
# en: {~You walk past. Your pride is intact, and so is your empty purse.|Another month, you tell yourself. You have a button left.}
opt.right.say.1 [5fff98] = {~你走了过去。你的自尊完好无损，你的空钱袋也是。|再等一个月，你对自己说。你还剩一颗纽扣。}

@event aid_interview
# en: The Bursar Will See You
title [7f82b3] = 财务官要见你
# en: The bursar has your forms open under her hand and a ledger the size of a tombstone at her elbow. "The fund is small," she says, "and the hands are many. Tell me why it should be yours. Or, if you'd rather not beg, I can lend you sixty crowns against your future, at no interest."
text [17eea6] = 财务官一只手按着你的申请表，手肘边是一本墓碑那么大的账簿。“基金很少，”她说，“伸手的人很多。告诉我为什么该给你。或者，如果你不想求人，我可以以你的前途作抵押借给你六十克朗，不收利息。”
# en: A small cluttered office, a grey-haired bursar behind a ledger as large as a tombstone, a student sitting very upright on a hard chair.
scene [9486c8] = 一间狭小杂乱的办公室，一位灰发的财务官坐在一本墓碑大小的账簿后面，一个学生笔直地坐在一张硬椅子上。
# en: Make your case
opt.left.label [d1740a] = 陈述你的理由
# en: You tell her plainly, and she listens without pity, which helps. "One term," she says, and stamps it. "Come back if it's still hard." Walking out, you feel both lighter and smaller.
opt.left.say.1 [5528de] = 你直截了当地说了，她听着，不带怜悯，这反倒有帮助。“一个学期，”她说着盖了章。“如果还是困难，再来。”走出去时，你觉得轻松了，也觉得自己变小了。
# en: She hears you out, and then reads you the list of people ahead of you. Some of their circumstances are worse. "Next year," she says, kindly. You almost wish she hadn't been kind.
opt.left.say.2 [fc9f6d] = 她听你说完，然后把排在你前面的人的名单念给你听。有些人的情况更糟。“明年吧，”她和气地说。你几乎希望她没那么和气。
# en: Take the loan
opt.right.label [e30491] = 接受贷款
# en: Sixty crowns, counted out in old coins, and your name in the tombstone ledger. "Eight a month, when you can, and a little less at the end," she says. "I'm a patient woman. The ledger is more patient still." It sits on your shoulder from then on.
opt.right.say.1 [4e2ca5] = 六十克朗，用旧硬币数给你，你的名字记进了墓碑账簿。“每月八克朗，付得起的时候再付，最后一次少一点，”她说，“我是个有耐心的女人。账簿比我更有耐心。”从那以后，它一直压在你肩上。

@event favour_vey_letter
# en: A Discreet Errand
title [14d2e3] = 一件隐秘的差事
# en: Professor Vey stops you in an empty corridor with a sealed letter and a silver coin. "A letter for the village. The house with the blue shutters. Into the hand of whoever opens the door, and not a word." Her smile is magnificent and gives nothing away.
text [adde6b] = 维伊教授在一条空走廊里拦住你，手里拿着一封封好的信和一枚银币。“一封送到村里的信。蓝色百叶窗的那户人家。交到开门的人手里，一个字也别说。”她的笑容光彩夺目，却什么也没透露。
# en: A professor in a violet coat holding out a sealed letter and a silver coin between two gloved fingers, in an empty theatre corridor.
scene [6d6c0c] = 一位穿紫罗兰色外套的教授在空荡荡的剧场走廊里，用戴着手套的两根手指递出一封封好的信和一枚银币。
# en: Deliver it, unread
opt.left.label [edeb48] = 送去，不看
# en: The house with the blue shutters is at the far end of the village, in the rain. An old man opens the door, reads the name on the letter and starts to cry. You walk back soaked and never ask.
opt.left.say.1 [1431e1] = 蓝色百叶窗的那户人家在村子最远的一头，下着雨。一位老人开了门，看了看信上的名字，哭了起来。你浑身湿透地走回去，从来没有问过。
# en: Hold it up to the light first
opt.right.label [eda50a] = 先对着光看一眼
# en: You make out one line: "...I have never stopped..." Then you deliver it. The next day Vey says, without looking at you, "The light in that corridor is very good, isn't it?"
opt.right.say.1 [8662e4] = 你辨认出一行字：“……我从未停止……”然后你把信送到了。第二天，维伊教授看都没看你一眼就说：“那条走廊的光线真好，不是吗？”

@event favour_thorne_marking
# en: Forty Essays
title [fcfc15] = 四十篇论文
# en: Professor Thorne puts forty first-year essays on your desk. "Mark them. A crown for every five. Be honest. Honesty is a kindness they will not thank you for." He leaves. The first essay begins, "Fire is hot."
text [0ac70d] = 索恩教授把四十篇一年级生的论文放在你桌上。“批改。每五篇一克朗。要诚实。诚实是一种他们不会感激的仁慈。”他走了。第一篇的开头是：“火是热的。”
# en: A stack of forty first-year essays on a desk under a lamp, a red pen, a student with an expression of growing despair.
scene [e38153] = 灯下桌上一摞四十篇一年级生的论文，一支红笔，一个越来越绝望的学生。
# en: Mark them honestly
opt.left.label [5bc996] = 诚实地批改
# en: Forty essays, eleven of them good, one brilliant and the rest about how fire is hot. Thorne reads your marks and says "Hm." You've learned that "Hm" is pay too.
opt.left.say.1 [a64129] = 四十篇论文，十一篇不错，一篇出色，其余都在讲火是热的。索恩教授看了你的批改，说了声“嗯”。你已经明白，“嗯”也算一种报酬。
# en: Mark them kindly
opt.right.label [f8616f] = 宽厚地批改
# en: You give every first-year a word of encouragement. Thorne raises your marks on three and lowers them on twenty. "Kindness," he says, "is not the same as a pass." He pays you anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [475d7f] = 你给每个一年级生都写了一句鼓励的话。索恩教授把其中三篇的分数提高了，二十篇压低了。“仁慈，”他说，“和及格不是一回事。”他还是付了你钱。

@event favour_amaranth_shift
# en: The Night Shift
title [99806e] = 夜班
# en: Sister Amaranth needs a pair of hands for the infirmary's night shift. "Basins, bandages, and sitting with whoever can't sleep. Eight crowns. Don't faint. If you faint, you're a patient, and patients don't get paid."
text [bcef7e] = 阿玛兰斯修女需要一双手帮医务室值夜班。“端盆、换绷带，陪着睡不着的人。八克朗。别晕倒。晕倒了你就是病人，病人可拿不到钱。”
# en: A dim infirmary ward at night, a student in an apron carrying a basin between rows of beds, a stern healer writing by a single lamp.
scene [6cb985] = 夜里昏暗的医务室病房，一个系着围裙的学生端着水盆走在一排排病床之间，一位严厉的治疗师在一盏灯下写字。
# en: Take the shift
opt.left.label [384351] = 值这个夜班
# en: A first-year with a fever, a prefect with a broken wrist, a boy who just wants someone awake. By dawn you're grey with tiredness. Amaranth says, "Keep doing that," and pays you.
opt.left.say.1 [f40aef] = 一个发烧的一年级生，一个手腕骨折的级长，一个只是想有人醒着陪他的男孩。到了天亮，你累得脸色发灰。阿玛兰斯修女说“继续这样做”，然后付了你钱。
# en: Offer to roll bandages by day instead
opt.right.label [a37891] = 提出白天来卷绷带
# en: She looks at you over her spectacles and hands you a mountain of linen. "Bandages it is. Less pay, all of the tedium." By the end you could roll them in your sleep.
opt.right.say.1 [a6e389] = 她从眼镜上方看了你一眼，递给你一大堆亚麻布。“那就卷绷带。报酬少些，枯燥一点不少。”到最后你闭着眼都能卷。

@event upper_year_errands
# en: Errands for Upper-Years
title [a1842a] = 替高年级跑腿
# en: {Upper-years pay for errands, a book fetched or a queue stood in or a letter carried to the owlery.|An upper-year waves a list and a coin at you. Word has got round.|"You again," says the upper-year, pleased. "Good. The usual, plus my laundry."} {~The list is long.|The coin is small.|One item on the list just says "find my cat".}
text [51e0a0] = {高年级生会付钱让人跑腿，取本书，排个队，或者把信送到猫头鹰塔。|一个高年级生冲你挥着一张清单和一枚硬币。消息已经传开了。|“又是你，”高年级生高兴地说，“好。老样子，再加上我的脏衣服。”}{~清单很长。|硬币很小。|清单上有一项只写着“找到我的猫”。}
# en: A crowded common room, a lounging upper-year holding out a coin and a list, a younger student taking the list with a sigh.
scene [6dbb95] = 一间拥挤的公共休息室，一个懒洋洋的高年级生递出一枚硬币和一张清单，一个低年级生叹着气接过清单。
# en: Run the errands
opt.left.label [54caa0] = 去跑腿
# en: {~You run up and down the towers all evening and are paid in coins and condescension.|You fetch, carry and queue. Your legs are tired; your purse is less light.}
opt.left.say.1 [9529cb] = {~你一整晚在塔楼间上上下下，拿到的报酬是硬币加居高临下。|你取东西、搬东西、排队。腿累了，钱袋没那么轻了。}
# en: Name your price
opt.right.label [979a40] = 开个价
# en: {~"More, or find your own cat." They pay. You find the cat anyway; it was in the laundry.|You haggle like a merchant's child. The upper-year pays with grudging respect.}
opt.right.say.1 [f2b367] = {~“加钱，不然自己找猫去。”他们付了。你还是把猫找到了，就在脏衣服堆里。|你像商人家的孩子一样讨价还价。高年级生不情不愿地带着几分佩服付了钱。}
# en: {~"Never mind," says the upper-year, and gives the list to a first-year behind you. Word gets round of that too.|They laugh, and find someone cheaper. You keep your dignity and nothing else.}
opt.right.say.2 [15586d] = {~“算了，”高年级生说着，把清单给了你身后的一个一年级生。这件事也传开了。|他们笑了，找了个更便宜的人。你保住了尊严，别的什么也没留下。}

@event pawnbroker_window
# en: The Pawnbroker's Window
title [8d463b] = 当铺的橱窗
# en: {The pawnbroker's window is full of other people's treasures, wands and rings and a stuffed owl. The sign says "Fair prices. Redemption within the year."|{flag(pawned_something): The pawnbroker's window again. Something of yours is in it now.|The pawnbroker's window again, the same treasures in new places.}|The pawnbroker nods at you through the glass like an acquaintance.} {~A first-year's silver locket is in the front row.|There's a familiar's collar, empty.|The stuffed owl seems to judge you.}
text [d77be4] = {当铺的橱窗里满是别人的宝贝，魔杖、戒指，还有一只猫头鹰标本。招牌上写着“价格公道，一年内可赎回”。|{flag(pawned_something): 又是当铺的橱窗。现在里面有一件是你的东西。|又是当铺的橱窗，还是那些宝贝，换了位置。}|当铺老板隔着玻璃冲你点点头，像个熟人。}{~一个一年级生的银挂坠摆在第一排。|有一个魔宠项圈，空的。|那只猫头鹰标本好像在评判你。}
# en: A dusty village shop window crowded with pawned treasures, wands, rings and a stuffed owl, a student looking in with their hands in empty pockets.
scene [4f25be] = 村里一扇积满灰尘的店铺橱窗，挤满了典当来的宝贝，魔杖、戒指和一只猫头鹰标本，一个学生双手插在空口袋里往里看。
# en: Pawn something you'd miss
opt.left.label [5697a9] = 当掉一件你会想念的东西
# en: {~Your good boots, or your grandmother's ring, or the wand-case with your name burned in it. The money is fair; the ticket says "within the year". You put the ticket somewhere safe and try not to look at it.|You hand over something you love, and take the money, and walk home faster than usual.}
opt.left.say.1 [2e7b7f] = {~你的好靴子，或者祖母的戒指，或者烙着你名字的魔杖盒。钱给得公道；当票上写着“一年内”。你把当票收在稳妥的地方，尽量不去看它。|你交出一件心爱的东西，接过钱，走回家的步子比平常快。}
# en: Walk on
opt.right.label [383259] = 走过去
# en: {~You walk on with your hands in your pockets. They're empty, but they're yours.|Not today. The owl watches you go.}
opt.right.say.1 [502b0d] = {~你双手插在口袋里走了过去。口袋是空的，但它们是你的。|今天不了。那只猫头鹰目送你离开。}
